    "subtitle": "How Korea became free and built a new country.",
    "body": "Long ago, Korea was not free. Another country ruled the land for many years. People could not use their own flag. They could not speak freely.\n\nBut the people never gave up hope. They wished for a free country every day.\n\nAt last, the great day came. On August 15, 1945, Korea won its liberation. The hard rule was over. People ran into the streets and cheered. They <mark>waved the flag</mark> with happy tears. Bells rang, and songs filled the air.\n\nBut the work was not finished yet. The country still needed a new government. So on August 15, 1948, the Republic of Korea was born. That day, a free nation truly began.",
